{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"your-first-component","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your first component"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A button, with a hover state and a second variant. Everything below is one file,\nand the tabs show what the compiler made of it: the CSS and the class names on\nthis page came out of the compiler, not out of prose."}]},{"type":"component","name":"example","attributes":{"name":"button-variants"},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-to-notice","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What to notice"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The condition lives inside the value."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"backgroundColor","source":"backgroundColor"}},{"type":"text","value":" is written once, with\nits resting value and its hover value together:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"backgroundColor: {\n  base: \"light-dark(oklch(0.21 0 0), oklch(0.92 0 0))\",\n  \":hover\": \"light-dark(oklch(0.31 0 0), oklch(0.85 0 0))\",\n}","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-property\">backgroundColor</span>: {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">base</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;light-dark(oklch(0.21 0 0), oklch(0.92 0 0))&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;:hover&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;light-dark(oklch(0.31 0 0), oklch(0.85 0 0))&quot;</span>,\n}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You never look in two places to find out what colour a button is."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Colours are "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">light-dark</span>()","source":"light-dark()"}},{"type":"text","value":" pairs."}]},{"type":"text","value":" There is no dark variant, no "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">dark:</span>","source":"dark:"}},{"type":"text","value":" prefix\nand no second stylesheet. The browser picks the half that matches the page's\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"color-scheme","source":"color-scheme"}},{"type":"text","value":", which the app sets once on "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">html</span>&gt;","source":"<html>"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second variant is a second handle."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={[styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">base</span>, styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">quiet</span>]}","source":"sx={[styles.base, styles.quiet]}"}},{"type":"text","value":"\nmerges them in order, and the merge happens "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per entry"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the quiet style's base\ncolour replaces the first one's base colour, and its hover colour replaces the\nhover colour. Everything it does not mention (the padding, the radius, the font)\nis still there. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/merging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merging"}]},{"type":"text","value":" has the rule, and how to drop an\nentry you did not name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One class per declaration."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Open the CSS tab: every rule is one class with a\nsingle declaration. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/start/how-it-works#the-pipeline","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How it works"}]},{"type":"text","value":" explains\nwhy that keeps the stylesheet small."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/start/how-it-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How it works"}]},{"type":"text","value":": what happens between the file and\nthe stylesheet."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/start/mental-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mental model"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the five ideas the rest builds on."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"your-first-component","text":"Your first component","level":1},{"id":"what-to-notice","text":"What to notice","level":2},{"id":"next","text":"Next","level":2}]}
